## 1. Full physical operators, reflection and signs

Use the proposal's M=2n>=4, B=sum n_j, p_m=|1^m0^(M-m)>, and J equal to reversal followed by a bit flip on every site. Reversal and the simultaneous flips commute; J is unitary, self-adjoint and squares to identity. On the full battery,

    J n_j J=I-n_(M+1-j),  JY_jJ=-Y_(M+1-j),
    JBJ=M I-B.

For j=2,...,M-1 the two control projectors in F_j=n_(j-1)Y_j(I-n_(j+1)) commute with Y_j. Therefore F_j is Hermitian with norm one, and it acts only on the declared consecutive triple. Direct evaluation on every prefix gives F_j p_(j-1)=i p_j, F_j p_j=-i p_(j-1), and zero otherwise. Every individual F_j therefore preserves the entire prefix span, not merely the intended trajectory. This is stronger than what was needed for the parent's unfiltered ordered nY gates and is not obtained by projecting a physical operation afterward.

Conjugation by J changes F_j to

    -(I-n_(M+2-j))Y_(M+1-j)n_(M-j)
       =-F_(M+1-j),

where the distinct-site factors commute. This proves the proposed full-space identity, including the minus sign. With a=n+k+1 and b=n-k, reflection exchanges a and b, so G_k=F_a-F_b commutes with J on the full 2^M-dimensional battery. No implementation of J is needed or supplied.

On s_0=p_n, G_0 produces i(p_(n-1)+p_(n+1))=i sqrt(2)s_1. Acting on s_1 gives -i sqrt(2)s_0. For k>=1, the outward action on the low branch comes from -F_b and on the high branch from F_a; both signs are +i. Thus G_k s_k=i s_(k+1), G_k s_(k+1)=-i s_k, with zero action on the other s_l. Dividing only the center by nu_0=sqrt(2) makes every A_k the usual Y on its indicated two-dimensional quotient edge. The desired even span is invariant for all real angles, including angles outside the nominal interval. No F_1 or F_M is used.

The global and promised-domain norm statements must remain different. On the even span ||A_k||=1. The full-space triangle bound ||A_k||<=2/nu_k is safe. In fact for k>=1 the two triple supports are disjoint and their F terms have independent eigenvalues +/-1, so ||A_k||=2 on the full space. A global error bound eta is therefore not available merely from the restricted norm-one statement. The source correctly uses a larger full-space residual bound.

Two analytic discriminators make these signs and domains consequential. Omitting the center normalization changes the central rotation angle to sqrt(2)theta_0; mean energy can still be exactly n while the packet is wrong. Replacing F_a-F_b by F_a+F_b sends the center toward the *antisymmetric* branch. For M=4, theta_0=pi/4, the resulting vector differs from the desired packet by norm one, even though its mean number remains two. Mean-energy agreement alone does not verify packet preparation or the mirror sign.

